\description{
This function conducts the likelihood-based sensitivity analysis for publication bias
on the time-dependent SROC curve and SAUC in meta-analysis of prognostic studies.
At each time point, the time-dependent sensitivity and specificity are reconstructed from the published
survival probabilities of the test-positive and test-negative groups (Combescure et al., 2016).
The logit-transformed sensitivity, specificity, and the log hazard ratio (lnHR) are modeled by
the trivariate random-effects model,
combined with a selection function on the \eqn{t}-statistic of lnHR.
The model is fitted for each time point in \code{time.points} and
each marginal selection probability \eqn{p} in \code{senp.p}.
}
\details{
\describe{
\item{Time-dependent sensitivity and specificity}{At time \eqn{t},
\eqn{\mathrm{Se}(t) = (1 - S_1(t)) q_1 / ((1 - S_1(t)) q_1 + (1 - S_0(t)) q_0)}{Se(t) = (1 - S1(t)) q1 / ((1 - S1(t)) q1 + (1 - S0(t)) q0)}
and
\eqn{\mathrm{Sp}(t) = S_0(t) q_0 / (S_1(t) q_1 + S_0(t) q_0)}{Sp(t) = S0(t) q0 / (S1(t) q1 + S0(t) q0)},
where \eqn{S_1(t)}{S1(t)} and \eqn{S_0(t)}{S0(t)} are the survival probabilities of groups 1 and 0,
and \eqn{q_1 = n_1 / (n_1 + n_0)}{q1 = n1 / (n1 + n0)} and \eqn{q_0 = 1 - q_1}{q0 = 1 - q1}.
Survival probabilities of 1 and 0 are replaced by \eqn{(n + 0.5) / (n + 1)} and \eqn{0.5 / (n + 1)}.}
\item{Within-study variances and covariances}{They are calculated from the survival probabilities up to \eqn{t},
assuming the censoring distribution \eqn{G(t) = \exp(-\eta t)}{G(t) = exp(-eta * t)} common to all the studies.
\eqn{\eta}{eta} is estimated within [0, 1] by least squares from \code{data.mt}, such that
the pooled survival probability at the median follow-up time multiplied by \eqn{G} is close to 0.5.}
\item{Selection function}{The probability of publishing study \eqn{i} is modeled as
\eqn{\Phi(\alpha + \beta t_i)}{Phi(alpha + beta * t_i)}, where \eqn{t_i}{t_i} is lnHR divided by its standard error.
For given \eqn{p} and the other parameters, \eqn{\alpha}{alpha} is determined such that
the mean of the inverse of the marginal selection probabilities of the observed studies equals \eqn{1/p}.}
\item{SAUC}{The SROC curve and SAUC are calculated from the parameters of the
logit-transformed sensitivity and specificity. See \code{\link{sauc}}.}
}
}
